    "body": "## Description\n\nCreate a `docs/faq.md` file answering common questions new contributors and users might have about HoneyBee Browser.\n\n## Steps to Complete\n\n1. Create `docs/faq.md`.\n2. Answer at least these five questions in your own words:\n   - What is HoneyBee Browser?\n   - Is HoneyBee based on Chromium or Firefox?\n   - Do I need prior browser development experience to contribute?\n   - What programming languages will HoneyBee use?\n   - How do I get help if I'm stuck?\n3. Use a clean markdown structure with `##` headers for each question.\n4. Link to it from the `README.md` (add an \"FAQ\" bullet under \"How to Contribute\").\n5. Commit with `docs: add FAQ page`.\n\n## Learning Outcomes\n\n- Technical writing.\n- Navigating and editing the repository structure.\n\n## Helpful Resources\n\n- [Google Chrome FAQ](https://www.google.com/chrome/faq/)\n- [Firefox FAQ](https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/firefox/faq/)\n",
